    "body": "> @sideshowbarker it seems we no longer have .inc resources, right?\r\n\r\nRight\r\n\r\n> Should we modify this to index \"source\" instead as HTML?\r\n\r\nTo just make GitHub see the `source` file as HTML, I think we don’t strictly need a `.gitattributes` at all—because as far as I can see, GitHub already seems to be doing that without us having configured it. But I suppose it doesn’t harm to make it explicit, so I raised PR #2091 for that.\r\n\r\nAnd I guess for the HTML `.gitattributes` we should make a change here regardless, since given that we no longer have any `.inc` files, the `.gitattributes` is currently doing nothing at all.\r\n\r\n> For other repositories, I guess it's unclear whether Bikeshed counts as HTML. Or for that matter whether `source` does.\r\n> (We might also want to deploy .gitattributes to other repositories, as a lot of them look like they just contain shell script to GitHub.)\r\n\r\nYeah, for BikeShed repos, as far as I can see from looking at the indicator the GitHub web UI shows for, e.g., https://github.com/whatwg/dom/ —where it’s not recognizing the `dom.bs` files as HTML—GitHub needs `.gitattributes` files with `*.bs linguist-language=HTML` for those.\r\n\r\nAnyway, as far as the HTML repo goes, PR #2091 updates the `.gitattributes` file to just have:\r\n\r\n    source text diff=html linguist-language=HTML\r\n\r\nI think neither the `text` part nor `linguist-language=HTML` there actually have any affect over what GitHub automatically already does for the `source` file now. And not sure what difference `diff=html` actually makes in `git diff` output, and if it’s what we really want. But I guess we can try it and see.\r\n\r\nAlternatively we could just update PR #2091 to remove `.gitattributes` from the repo.\r\n\r\n",
